CMSA augmented Cachegrind
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
This research branch adds bounded D1 counter streaming for the Cache Miss
Signal Analyzer. It supports:

- --d1-trace=off|ascii|binary|counter
- --d1-trace-file=<path>
- --d1-counter-size=<misses>
- --d1-ground-truth=yes|no

Use --d1-trace=counter --d1-ground-truth=no for bounded model-only collection.
Ground truth is optional and remains independent from the CMSA prediction
path. Build this branch with ./autogen.sh, ./configure, and make.

Provenance
~~~~~~~~~~
This repository is a fork of Valgrind 3.23.0. Every modification is confined to
the cachegrind/ directory, the build files, and this README. They were made in
two stages:

  Chao Jin <c.jin@uq.edu.au>, 2024-2025
    Temporal and spatial locality measurement, per-layer cache usage, and
    shadow-cache identification of compulsory, conflict and capacity misses
    for D1 and LL. This is the work behind --d1-ground-truth.
      added:    cachegrind/cg_helper.c, cachegrind/cu_annotate.in
      modified: cachegrind/cg_main.c, cachegrind/cg_sim.c, build files

  Mo'ath Qutaish <m.qutaish@uq.edu.au>, 2026
    Bounded D1 counter-period streaming for CMSA (--d1-trace=counter and
    --d1-counter-size), which emits fixed-size counter records rather than an
    unbounded per-miss trace.
      modified: cachegrind/cg_sim.c, cachegrind/cg_main.c

Everything outside cachegrind/ and the build files is unmodified upstream
Valgrind.

